## UIKit Components (Django Cotton)

**CRITICAL**: All UIKit components MUST use the `c-uikit.` prefix, NOT `c-` directly.

### Component Naming Convention

- ✅ **Correct**: `<c-uikit.button>`, `<c-uikit.badge>`, `<c-uikit.input>`, `<c-uikit.alert>`
- ❌ **Incorrect**: `<c-button>`, `<c-badge>`, `<c-input>`, `<c-alert>`

### Available Components

1. **Buttons** (`c-uikit.button`)
   - Variants: default, destructive, outline, secondary, ghost, link
   - Sizes: xs, sm, default, lg, icon
   - Supports `href` attribute to render as link

2. **Badges** (`c-uikit.badge`)
   - Variants: default, secondary, destructive, outline

3. **Inputs** (`c-uikit.input`)
   - Types: text, email, password, number
   - States: normal, disabled

4. **Form Components**
   - `c-uikit.form.field` - Container for form elements
   - `c-uikit.form.label` - Form labels
   - `c-uikit.form.description` - Helper text
   - `c-uikit.form.error` - Error messages
   - `c-uikit.form.fieldset` - Fieldset wrapper

5. **Links** (`c-uikit.a`)
   - Styled anchor links with hover effects

6. **Alerts** (`c-uikit.alert`)
   - Variants: default, destructive
   - Sub-components: `c-uikit.alert.title`, `c-uikit.alert.description`

7. **Command Palette** (`c-uikit.command`)
   - Sub-components: `c-uikit.command.input`, `c-uikit.command.list`, `c-uikit.command.empty`, `c-uikit.command.group`, `c-uikit.command.item`, `c-uikit.command.separator`

### Component Features

UIKit components automatically handle:
- **SVG Icon Styling**: SVG elements inside components are automatically styled with `size-4` and proper spacing (no need to add `w-4 h-4` classes)
- **Link Support**: Components with `href` attribute automatically render as `<a>` tags instead of `<button>`
- **Attribute Forwarding**: All HTML attributes (like `href`, `id`, `class`, etc.) are properly forwarded to the rendered element
- **Variant Support**: Components support multiple variants (default, outline, destructive, secondary, ghost, link)
- **Size Support**: Many components support size variants (xs, sm, default, lg, icon)

### Usage Examples

```django
<!-- Basic button -->
<c-uikit.button variant="default" size="lg">Click Me</c-uikit.button>

<!-- Button as link -->
<c-uikit.button href="{% url 'home' %}" variant="outline">Go Home</c-uikit.button>

<!-- Button with icon (SVG automatically styled) -->
<c-uikit.button variant="outline">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10.5 19.5 3 12m0 0 7.5-7.5M3 12h18" />
    </svg>
    Back
</c-uikit.button>

<!-- Badge -->
<c-uikit.badge variant="secondary">Badge</c-uikit.badge>

<!-- Alert -->
<c-uikit.alert variant="destructive">
    <c-uikit.alert.title>Error</c-uikit.alert.title>
    <c-uikit.alert.description>Something went wrong</c-uikit.alert.description>
</c-uikit.alert>
```

### Component Location

UIKit components are located in:
```
src/vouch/templates/cotton/uikit/[component-name]/index.html
```

